 ;; ── context — why ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :context
 {:problem "The on-chain LandRegistry records only DONATED waqf-inalienable land (starts at 0); no upstream actor measured how much of the world's land we have data on, who holds it, or where the 取-concentration is. The legacy crawler→land-owners→maps design was RDBMS/KV and never built."
  :role "Data-acquisition feeder of the land-sovereignty stack (ADR-2605192100 §1.11 + 2605192245); land-scale sibling of the KG-mirror lineage (inochi/tsumugi/kabuto/kanae/keizu), clj-native on the kotoba Datom log."}

 ;; ── decision — D1..D7 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :decision
 {:D1 "Multi-SOURCE, source-agnostic ingest ({:owners :parcels}); per-source normalize → committed snapshot → kotoba Datom log. Sources: Wikidata parks/reserves/buildings, NYC PLUTO gov cadastre, FR DVF values, GLEIF company identity, OSM building stock + Wikidata country-area denominator."
  :D2 "REFRAMED public-record gate (the constitution does NOT ban personal data; Rider v3.1 §2(c)/ADR-2606082400 bans ASYMMETRIC/MONETIZED surveillance, affirms reciprocal-symmetric 相互監視): P1 public-record provenance + P2 reciprocal/symmetric + P3 map-not-target/non-monetized. Per-jurisdiction grounding (jurisdiction.cljc): bulk-public juris (SE/US/GB/IE/NL/NO) ingest natural persons; per-parcel-only (JP/KR) and restricted (DE/AT/CH/FR owner-names) do not; unknown degrades honestly."
  :D3 "INGEST vs PUBLISH distinct: gate permits ingest; the published analytical artifact applies publish-prudence — bulk-cadastre ORDINARY individuals anonymized (sha256-key, no name, raw stays local/IPFS cold-tier); NOTABLE public-figure owners from open KGs (Wikidata, already-public QID) ARE represented. No dwelling coordinates (G1)."
  :D4 "Per-source RELIABILITY (信頼度) tiers + trust-weighted cross-source reconcile (GLEIF authoritative name wins over Wikidata crowd label, disagreement recorded); as-of DIFF (差分) feeds the append-only log; sanitize (parcel > country area dropped, G4)."
  :D5 "Content-addressing (cid.cljc CIDv1 raw/sha2-256, verified ipfs-compatible) + integrity verify.cljc (committed-only) + UNIFIED canonical Datom log (emit_all.cljc, source-tagged) + capstone digest.cljc."
  :D6 "Storage: git-committed working copies + IPFS-pinned (clean public bundle DHT-announced); raw + resolution caches committed so a rebuild never re-queries; full DataLad superdataset + remote IPFS pin = operator cold-tier (ADR-2605241500). 負担をかけない: one polite fetch per increment; the loop re-ingests committed snapshots with zero network I/O."
  :D7 "PRODUCTION-SCALE (R2, scale_ingest.cljc + PRODUCTION.md): bounded-memory line-streaming for full bulk (PLUTO ~860k / nationwide DVF), aggregates byte-identical to the sample path, person names anonymized on the fly; operator runs the one-shot bulk download, never the loop."
  :G3 "jinushi asserts NO transfer/mint/donation — only the on-chain LandRegistry moves land, by member donation (no-server-key)."}

 :invariants
 ["public-record + reciprocal-symmetric + map-not-target + non-monetized (G1/Rider §2(c))"
  "bulk-cadastre ordinary-person names NEVER in the public repo (gitignored; local/IPFS cold-tier)"
  "non-adjudicating; concentration/coverage = transient aggregates (G2)"
  "sourcing honesty: LAND coverage = national-park (protected-public-land) ÷ world land, NOT all-land (G4)"
  "no transfer/mint asserted (G3)"
  "Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000) — narration not introduced; pure data methods"
  "kotoba Datom = canonical state (ADR-2605262130 / 2605312345)"
  "Apache-2.0 + Charter Rider"]

